<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<chapter xml:id="ch17-exterior-derivatives" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Exterior Derivatives: Gradient, Curl, and Divergence Revisited</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>The forms and pullbacks of Chapter 16 are now ready to be differentiated. Starting with the familiar differential of a function, we define the exterior derivative of work and flux forms and explain its relation to gradient, curl, and divergence. Continuous mixed partial derivatives explain why applying this derivative twice gives zero; the domain determines whether a closed form has a global potential.</p>
  </introduction>

